=== PARITY (web source reproduced end-to-end) ===
  - Data sources (web useTranslation + useMutation): bound through the P1/S8 seam
    BackendToolRunner→BackendToolModel. run() mirrors mutation.mutate(); the runner
    fires POST/GET/DELETE /dev-tools/{endpoint} (web apiFetch) and reports a
    BackendToolRunOutcome (success json / failure message / offline). No HTTP in the view.
  - Composition (web ToolCard + Run Button + Badge + ResultPanel):
      • ToolCard  -> TSGlassPanel + TSIconBox(tone) + title/description (rendered
                     verbatim, as web renders its props).
      • Run Button-> TSButton(variant:.primary,size:.small,isLoading:phase==.running)
                     + play.fill glyph (web `Play`); web `t('Run')`.
      • Badge     -> tinted dot pill, danger/success tone, web `t('Failed')/t('Success')`,
                     shown only once a result settles (web `mutation.data && <Badge/>`).
      • ResultPanel-> error (rose text + retry) | pretty JSON (mono, scroll, TSCopyButton)
                     | idle "No result yet"; BackendToolJSON.prettyPrinted reproduces
                     JSON.stringify(data,null,2) (sorted keys + 2-space indent).
      • children  -> generic `extra` ViewBuilder slot.
  - States (ALL rendered, each with a #if DEBUG preview + model unit test):
      loading (run in flight, skeleton) · empty (idle "No result yet") ·
      success (JSON + copy) · error (message + Retry) · stale (freshness chip +
      "Result may be out of date" banner, time-based) · offline (cached body kept +
      "Offline — showing last result" banner + offline chip).
  - i18n (P1/S10): web keys preserved verbatim — "Run" / "Success" / "Failed" +
    "No result yet"; native chrome namespaced devtools.tool.* (live/stale/offline/
    running/retry/copy/offlineBanner/staleBanner). Every code-referenced key is
    declared in BackendTool.strings; NO English string literals in native code
    (all via BackendToolStrings facade + Text(verbatim:)).
  - Accessibility: VoiceOver labels on Run (action + tool title), status badge,
    freshness chip, method chip, copy button, banners; result panel carries a
    combined summary; Dynamic-Type system fonts (Font.TS); reduce-motion honored
    (TSSkeleton shimmer + TSCopyButton).
  - Telemetry (P1/S11): BackendToolModel.start() emits view.opened with surface
    slug "BackendTool" exactly once (OSLogBackendToolTelemetry default; prod app
    injects the shared diagnostics adapter).

